.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a model‑agnostic prompt container used by all IModelBackend implementations and embedded models\&. 

An \fBIModelPromp<T>\fP encapsulates the raw prompt, contextual metadata, session information, backend parameters, and optional tags\&. 
.br
 It provides a unified structure for passing input into any model pipeline, regardless of modality or backend type\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The underlying prompt type (e\&.g\&., text, tokens, bytes, AST, etc\&.)\&. 
.RE
.PP

